{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776850960,"nonce":"xdiPzkHvrHfBepNoE5TL1u3B9fU=","title":"Support overflow mode for reviewer sessions","message":"## Problem\n\nCurrently overflow mode is explicitly skipped for review sessions (`launch.py:209-218`):\n\n```python\n# Check overflow flag file — skip overflow for review sessions so the\n# review agent always uses its own provider (e.g. Claude Code).\noverflow = None\nif not names[\"is_review\"]:\n    ...\n```\n\nThis forces reviews to always use the primary agent (e.g., Claude Code), even when the user wants to use a cheaper model for both coding AND reviewing.\n\n## Use Case\n\nWhen Claude auth is broken or the user wants to save costs, they should be able to run reviews with the overflow provider (e.g., Codex/OpenAI) instead of manually editing REVIEW.md.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\n1. Add `overflow` section support to REVIEW.md (same schema as WORKFLOW.md)\n2. When overflow flag is set AND REVIEW.md has overflow config, use it for reviews\n3. If REVIEW.md has no overflow section, fall back to current behavior (use REVIEW.md's agent.kind)\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- `host/launch.py` — remove `if not names[\"is_review\"]:` guard, check REVIEW.md's overflow config\n- `core/config/loader.py` — ensure overflow section is parsed from REVIEW.md (should already work)\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_launch_uses_overflow_for_review_when_configured`\n- `test_launch_skips_overflow_for_review_when_not_configured`\n\nREQ: REQ-031 (dual-agent workflow)","files":null}]}